{
  "analysis": "I now understand the kit's language and structure. The README describes a task queue system with Ready/In Progress/Blocked/Done sections. HEARTBEAT.md outlines the workflow. cron_plan.json has basic jobs but needs to be updated with the priority ordering. I need to check the existing memory and tasks directories, then create/update the required files.",
  "plan": "Check the contents of the memory and tasks directories to see what exists. Then I'll create/update: 1) tasks/QUEUE.md with task sections and example tasks, 2) memory/daily_progress_template.md, 3) update cron_plan.json with priority ordering (human requests > urgent blockers > Ready tasks).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la tasks/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la memory/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat tasks/* 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat memory/* 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The files have been created successfully. The cron_plan.json size increased from 422 to 1892 bytes, and memory directory size increased from 35 to 73 bytes. Now I need to verify that all files were created correctly with the proper content.",
